      },
      "inLanguage": "en-GB",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/range-rover/vogue-old-mk-3#faq-question-1",
          "name": "What engines did the Range Rover Vogue MK3 come with?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The L322 was offered with several engines across its production run, including the early BMW-derived TD6 diesel, the later Jaguar-derived TDV8 diesel, and petrol V8s ranging from the 4.4-litre AJ V8 to the supercharged AJ133. The engine fitted depends on the model year and trim."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/range-rover/vogue-old-mk-3#faq-question-2",
          "name": "Is the Range Rover L322 reliable?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Reliability varies significantly by engine and age. The TD6 is known for swirl flap and turbo issues, while the TDV8 can suffer from timing chain wear if servicing is neglected. With regular maintenance and prompt attention to warning signs, many L322s cover very high mileages."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/range-rover/vogue-old-mk-3#faq-question-3",
          "name": "How much does it cost to rebuild an L322 engine?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Cost depends on the engine variant and the extent of the damage, ranging from a targeted repair to a full rebuild. We provide a fixed quote after inspection, so you know the exact cost before any work is authorised."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/range-rover/vogue-old-mk-3#faq-question-4",
          "name": "Are parts still available for the Vogue MK3?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Despite its age, the L322 remains well supported through reconditioned units, used parts and aftermarket suppliers, and we maintain established relationships across the UK to source what's needed."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/range-rover/vogue-old-mk-3#faq-question-5",
          "name": "Should I repair or replace my L322 engine?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It depends on the fault, the mileage, and the car's overall condition. We'll always give an honest recommendation , sometimes a repair is the right call, other times a reconditioned or used engine replacement offers better long-term value."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/range-rover/vogue-old-mk-3#faq-question-6",
          "name": "Do you collect the vehicle or do I need to bring it in?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "We offer nationwide collection and delivery, so you don't need to be local to our workshop to use our services. Alternatively, you're welcome to drop the car off yourself."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/range-rover/vogue-old-mk-3#faq-question-7",
          "name": "Is there a warranty on reconditioned or replacement engines?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, every reconditioned and replacement engine we fit is covered by a warranty, giving you peace of mind after the work is complete."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/range-rover/vogue-old-mk-3#faq-question-8",
          "name": "How long does an L322 engine rebuild or replacement take?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Timescales vary depending on parts availability and the scope of work, but most rebuilds and replacements are completed within one to two weeks. We'll confirm a realistic timeframe once we've inspected the vehicle."
          }
        }
